brainCUT bundles the following libraries. Each keeps its own license; the texts are in
node_modules/<package>/LICENSE after an install.

mediabunny — demuxing, muxing and the WebCodecs wrappers
MPL-2.0
https://github.com/Vanilagy/mediabunny

pixi.js — WebGL compositing
MIT
https://github.com/pixijs/pixijs

pixi-filters — the effect filters built on top of it
MIT
https://github.com/pixijs/filters

gl-transitions — the GLSL transitions
MIT
https://github.com/gl-transitions/gl-transitions
Each transition names its own author in the header of its GLSL source, and that credit is
kept in the shader as it is compiled.

immer — immutable drafts and the patches the undo stack is built from
MIT
https://github.com/immerjs/immer

idb-keyval — the IndexedDB wrapper projects and recents are stored through
Apache-2.0
https://github.com/jakearchibald/idb-keyval

tinykeys — the keyboard shortcut bindings
MIT
https://github.com/jamiebuilds/tinykeys

bezier-easing — cubic bezier interpolation for keyframes
MIT
https://github.com/gre/bezier-easing

gifenc — GIF encoding and palette quantization
MIT
https://github.com/mattdesl/gifenc

@ffmpeg/ffmpeg and @ffmpeg/util — the loader for the converter
MIT
https://github.com/ffmpegwasm/ffmpeg.wasm

Not part of this repository:

@ffmpeg/core — the ffmpeg build itself, WebAssembly
LGPL-2.1-or-later, GPL for some builds
https://github.com/ffmpegwasm/ffmpeg.wasm
The core is not shipped with brainCUT and is not committed here. It is downloaded from a
CDN at runtime, once, and only when a file uses codecs the browser cannot decode on its
own. The mirror is a preference and can be emptied, which turns conversion off entirely.
